# G12 — the compensated prime diagonal: what it gives, and what it provably does not

**The Riemann Hypothesis is not proved.**  Nothing was weakened or assumed:
`RiemannHypothesisFor` and every earlier statement are untouched, there is no
`sorry`/`admit`, no `axiom`, no postulate, no Boolean receipt, no numerical
evidence and no `@[implemented_by]` in any Lean source of this cycle.
`lake build RiemannAnalytic` succeeds (8091 jobs) and `#print axioms` on every
new theorem returns only `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.

The first unproved theorem in the chain requested by G12 is stated exactly at
the end of this report.

